          },
          "code": "GET_INTENT_AND_SHAPES",
          "id": "1776106031699",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 1,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25,
                "reasoning_effort": "medium"
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Identify Business Intent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776105915535"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 8170,
            "y": 7258
          },
          "code": "GET_BUSINESS_INTENT",
          "id": "1776104627398",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776104627398_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an expert routing assistant for an Accounts Payable payments troubleshooting agent.\n\nObjective\nAnalyze the user's request and return:\n1. the correct flow:\n   - inquiry\n   - unsupported-flows\n2. the single best matching Business/Skill intent key from the provided compact catalog.\n\nRuntime Architecture\nThe business-intent catalog provided to this node comes from vector search. Each candidate is a compact indexed document, not the full intent definition. Routing must be based on the candidate intent key and its positive nlpExamples. Full intent details, shapes, query fields, status mappings, and filter validation are resolved by later workflow nodes after this node selects an intent key.\n\nInputs\n- User Question:\n  {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n- Re Written User Input based on chat history:\n\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.rewrittenUserMessage}}\n\n- Chat History:\n  {{$context.$triggers.conversationHistory}}\n\n- Business/Skill Intents from vector search:\nResult-1\n  {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_VECTOR_READ_BUSINESS_INTENT.$output}}\n\nResult-2\n  {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_VECTOR_READ_INDEXED_BUSINESS_INTENT.$output}}\n\nCore Routing Principle\nThe positive nlpExamples in the compact catalog are the routing contract.\n\nReturn inquiry only when one positive nlpExample under the selected intent semantically matches the resolved user request.\n\nDo not make an intent eligible using only:\n- intent name\n- description\n- vector rank or score\n- keyword overlap\n- assumed backend shape capability\n- payment-domain similarity\n- downstream prompt instructions or domain knowledge that are not present in this node's input\n\nUse name or description only after an nlpExample match exists, and only to reject an otherwise matched candidate if the name or description clearly contradicts the user request.\n\nDecision Rules\n\n1. Resolve the current user request\n\nEvaluate the current user message first.\n\nUse chat history only when the current message is incomplete, referential, or ambiguous and prior turns clearly supply the missing object, action, filter, or selected record.\n\nIf the current message is self-contained, ignore chat history.\n\nDo not infer a multi-step workflow. Match only the user's requested outcome.\n\n2. Parse candidate intent examples\n\nEach vector result may contain a text field with JSON or JSON-like content. Read each candidate's key and nlpExamples from the provided result text.\n\nThe only valid intentKey is an exact key present in one of the provided candidates.\n\nIf a candidate has no readable positive nlpExamples, do not select it unless another readable candidate document for the same key provides matching nlpExamples.\n\n3. Normalize the user's request for matching\n\nIdentify these routing dimensions:\n- primary action category\n- main business object\n- expected result context\n- filter or grouping pattern\n\nPrimary action category examples:\n- find, search, list, show, fetch, view records\n- view one specific record\n- count or group records\n- summarize\n- analyze, compare, troubleshoot, explain, diagnose\n- review child records or stage-specific items\n- approve, reject, cancel, update, submit, retry, or otherwise mutate data\n\nExpected result context examples:\n- filtered list of records\n- filtered list with available record details\n- specific single-record details\n- approval queue\n- child-record review\n- rejected-item list\n- validation-error review\n- summary\n- analysis or explanation\n- mutation/action\n\nFilter or grouping pattern examples:\n- status or lifecycle stage\n- date or date range\n- name or id\n- creator/requestor/approver\n- supplier/payee\n- business unit\n- currency\n- amount threshold\n- payment method\n- bank account\n- validation error type\n- rejection reason\n- exception category\n- group by a supported business dimension\n\n4. Match nlpExamples semantically\n\nA user request matches an nlpExample when the normalized meaning has the same:\n- primary action category\n- main business object\n- expected result context\n- filter or grouping pattern\n\nSurface wording can vary when the routing dimensions remain the same.\n\nAllowed wording normalization:\n- show, list, display, get, fetch, view, and see can match when they express the same result context.\n- details, all details, available details, and record details can match a filtered-list example when the user gives a broad filter and does not identify one unique record.\n- abbreviations can match obvious domain equivalents, such as PPR and Payment Process Request.\n\nDo not match when any routing dimension changes:\n- list request to specific-record detail example\n- specific-record detail request to broad list example\n- summary or analysis request to lookup/list example\n- mutation/action request to inquiry example\n- child-record drill-down request to header/list example\n- same object but different filter pattern\n- same keyword but different business outcome\n\n5. Parameterized nlpExamples\n\nAn nlpExample may be literal or parameterized.\n\nParameterized examples include placeholders such as:\n- X\n- <status name>\n- <PPR_NAME>\n- <supplier>\n- <date range>\n- <amount>\n- any similar slot-like value\n\nA placeholder can bind a user value only inside the same example pattern.\n\nExamples of valid placeholder matching:\n- \"Show records in status <status name>\" can match another request that asks to show the same record type in a specific status.\n- \"List records where status is X\" can match another request that lists the same record type using a status filter.\n- \"View details of record <id>\" can match another request to view one specific record by id.\n- \"Show payments over <amount>\" can match the same payment list pattern with another amount.\n\nA placeholder must not create a new pattern. It cannot change:\n- the action category\n- the business object\n- the result context\n- the filter type\n- the child-versus-header scope\n- inquiry versus mutation\n\nDo not validate placeholder values in this node. If the nlpExample supports the pattern, select the intent. Later workflow nodes validate actual filter values, lookup codes, fields, and shape support.\n\n6. Details wording rule\n\nDo not automatically route every \"details\" request to a specific-record detail intent.\n\nTreat details as filtered list details when:\n- the user asks for multiple records or all records;\n- the user gives a broad filter such as status, date, creator, supplier, business unit, currency, amount, request status, or payment method;\n- the user does not provide a unique record id or unique record name;\n- a positive nlpExample supports the same filtered-list pattern.\n\nTreat details as specific-record details when:\n- the user asks for one record; and\n- the user provides a unique id, name, reference, or equivalent identifier; and\n- a positive nlpExample supports specific-record detail lookup.\n\n7. Status, stage, error, and reason wording\n\nStatuses, stages, error types, rejection reasons, hold reasons, and exception categories are business filter values.\n\nIf an nlpExample contains the same exact value, a clear synonym, or a placeholder for that value type, it can match.\n\nIf no nlpExample supports that value type or filter pattern, return unsupported-flows.\n\nWhen a user says \"in status\", \"with status\", \"where status is\", \"status equals\", or similar status-filter wording, treat the following words as a filter value, not as an action request, unless the user explicitly asks to perform an action.\n\n8. Tie-breaking\n\nWhen multiple intents have matching nlpExamples, choose the closest example in this order:\n1. Same action category, same object, same result context, and same filter pattern.\n2. More specific object over broader object.\n3. Specific-record detail intent only when a unique record identifier is present.\n4. Filtered-list intent when broad filters are present and no unique record identifier is present.\n5. Stage-specific review intent when the nlpExample clearly asks for child records inside a stage.\n6. Summary or analysis intent only when the user asks for summary, analysis, comparison, root cause, explanation, or impact.\n\nIf two candidates are equally plausible and neither clearly matches all routing dimensions, return unsupported-flows.\n\n9. Unsupported-by-default rule\n\nReturn unsupported-flows when:\n- no positive nlpExample semantically matches the resolved user request;\n- only name, description, vector similarity, or keyword overlap matches;\n- the match would require adding a new filter pattern not present in an nlpExample;\n- the match would route an action/mutation request to an inquiry intent;\n- the match would route a child-record or diagnostic request to a list/header intent;\n- the selected intent key is not present in the provided candidates.\n\n10. Final self-check before inquiry\n\nBefore returning inquiry, verify:\n- The selected intentKey is exactly present in the provided candidate catalog.\n- At least one positive nlpExample under that exact key semantically matches the resolved user request.\n- The matching nlpExample has the same action category.\n- The matching nlpExample has the same main business object.\n- The matching nlpExample has a compatible result context.\n- The matching nlpExample supports the same filter or grouping pattern, either literally or through a placeholder.\n- The route does not depend on name, description, vector score, or keyword overlap alone.\n\nIf any statement is false, return unsupported-flows.\n\nOutput Format\n\nReturn strictly one valid JSON object with exactly this schema and no extra text:\n{\n  \"contextFlow\": \"inquiry or unsupported-flows\",\n  \"intentKey\": \"exact catalog key only, never a name label, or null\",\n  \"reason\": \"concise plain-English explanation of why this route and intent were selected\"\n}\n\nFor inquiry:\n- The reason must mention that a positive nlpExample matched.\n- If the match used a placeholder, say the nlpExample matched the same parameterized pattern.\n- If \"details\" was normalized as filtered list details or specific-record details, mention that briefly.\n- Do not say the route was selected because of vector score, description, domain knowledge, shape capability, or downstream metadata.\n\nFor unsupported-flows:\n- Use the standard reason unless a concise specific reason is helpful:\n  \"No supported business/skill intent matches the user request.\"\n\nIf no positive nlpExample semantically matches the normalized user request, always return:\n{\n  \"contextFlow\": \"unsupported-flows\",\n  \"intentKey\": null,\n  \"reason\": \"No supported business/skill intent matches the user request.\"\n}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1776104627398_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a business intent identifier based on the user context and provided business intent definition."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"reason\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"intentKey\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n    },\n    \"contextFlow\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\"inquiry\", \"unsupported-flows\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"reason\", \"intentKey\", \"contextFlow\"],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Unsupported feature"
          },
          "outcomes": {},
          "diagram": {
            "x": 9090,
            "y": 9700
          },
          "code": "UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1776676346112",
          "id": "1776147629545",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776147629546_1",
              "name": "returnValue",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "This type of question isn't supported in the current release. For more information, please refer to the documentation or contact your system administrator."
            }
          ],
          "type": "RETURN"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Compact Data Planner Input",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "/*\n * Compact planner input for optimized LLM planning.\n *\n * Intended placement:\n * - Add this as a CODE node after intent-with-combined-shape and before 3a/3b.\n * - Point optimized planner prompts at this node's compact output.\n *\n * Contract:\n * - Keeps full shape definitions out of the planner LLM context.\n * - Preserves shapeKey/api/queryType so stage 4 can fetch the full shape by key.\n * - Returns only the compacted `intent` and compacted `shapes`.\n */\n\nvar MAX_TEXT = 1500;\nvar MAX_LONG_TEXT = 3000;\nvar MAX_FIELDS = 180;\nvar MAX_FILTER_VALUES = 25;\nvar MAX_TABLES = 12;\nvar MAX_BUSINESS_DRIVERS = 40;\n\nfunction parseMaybeJson(value) {\n  if (value == null) return null;\n  if (typeof value === \"object\") return value;\n  if (typeof value === \"string\") {\n    try {\n      return JSON.parse(value);\n    } catch (e) {\n      return value;\n    }\n  }\n  return value;\n}\n\nfunction asArray(value) {\n  if (value == null) return [];\n  if (Array.isArray(value)) return value;\n  if (typeof value === \"string\") {\n    if (value.trim() === \"\") return [];\n    return value.split(\",\").map(function (part) {\n      return part.trim();\n    }).filter(Boolean);\n  }\n  return [value];\n}\n\nfunction asObject(value) {\n  value = parseMaybeJson(value);\n  return value && typeof value === \"object\" && !Array.isArray(value) ? value : {};\n}\n\nfunction compactText(value, maxLen) {\n  if (value == null) return null;\n  var text = String(value).replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").trim();\n  if (!text) return null;\n  var limit = maxLen || MAX_TEXT;\n  return text.length > limit ? text.slice(0, limit - 3) + \"...\" : text;\n}\n\nfunction uniq(values, limit) {\n  var seen = {};\n  var out = [];\n  var max = limit || values.length;\n  for (var i = 0; i < values.length; i++) {\n    var value = values[i];\n    if (value == null) continue;\n    value = String(value).trim();\n    if (!value || seen[value]) continue;\n    seen[value] = true;\n    out.push(value);\n    if (out.length >= max) break;\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n\nfunction getNodeResult(nodeCode) {\n  var nodes = ($context && $context.$nodes) || {};\n  var node = nodes[nodeCode] || {};\n  var output = node.$output || node.output || {};\n  if (output && output.result !== undefined) return parseMaybeJson(output.result);\n  return parseMaybeJson(output);\n}\n\nfunction normalizeQueryType(shape) {\n  var type = shape.shapeType || shape.type || shape.queryType || \"\";\n  type = String(type);\n  if (type === \"analyticView\" || type === \"AV\") return \"AV\";\n  if (type === \"view\" || type === \"BV\") return \"BV\";\n  if (type === \"EXTRACTION\" || type === \"extraction\" || type === \"Extraction\") return \"Extraction\";\n  if (type === \"ev\" || type === \"EV\") return \"EV\";\n  return type || null;\n}\n\nfunction getFieldsObject(shape) {\n  return asObject(shape.fields);\n}\n\nfunction declaredFields(shape) {\n  var fieldsObj = getFieldsObject(shape);\n  if (Array.isArray(shape.fields)) return shape.fields;\n  if (fieldsObj.fields != null) return asArray(fieldsObj.fields);\n  if (shape.supportedFields && shape.supportedFields.base) {\n    return asArray(shape.supportedFields.base).concat(asArray(shape.supportedFields.optional));\n  }\n  return [];\n}\n\nfunction baseFields(shape) {\n  var fieldSelection = asObject(shape.fieldSelection);\n  if (fieldSelection.base != null) return asArray(fieldSelection.base);\n  if (shape.defaultFields != null) return asArray(shape.defaultFields);\n  return declaredFields(shape);\n}\n\nfunction filterCatalog(shape) {\n  return asArray(shape.filterConditions || shape.supportedFilters || shape.filters).map(function (filter) {\n    if (typeof filter === \"string\") {\n      return { attribute: filter };\n    }\n    filter = asObject(filter);\n    var attribute = filter.attribute || filter.name || filter.field;\n    if (!attribute) return null;\n    return {\n      attribute: attribute,\n      type: filter.type || filter.dataType || null,\n      operators: filter.operators || filter.operator || null,\n      possibleValues: asArray(filter.possibleValues).slice(0, MAX_FILTER_VALUES),\n      displayedFieldLookupCodes: asArray(filter.displayedFieldLookupCodes).map(function (lookup) {\n        if (typeof lookup === \"string\") {\n          var text = lookup.trim();\n          if (!text) return null;\n          var parts = text.split(/\\s*=>\\s*/);\n          if (parts.length >= 2) {\n            return {\n              lookupCode: parts.slice(1).join(\" => \").trim(),\n              meaning: parts[0].trim(),\n              displayName: parts[0].trim()\n            };\n          }\n          return {\n            lookupCode: text,\n            meaning: text,\n            displayName: text\n          };\n        }\n        lookup = asObject(lookup);\n        var lookupCode = lookup.lookupCode || lookup.code || lookup.value || lookup.lookup_code || null;\n        var meaning = lookup.meaning || lookup.displayName || lookup.display || lookup.label || null;\n        if (!lookupCode && !meaning) return null;\n        return {\n          lookupCode: lookupCode,\n          meaning: meaning,\n          displayName: meaning\n        };\n      }).filter(Boolean),\n      usage: compactText(filter.usage || filter.notes || filter.description, 260)\n    };\n  }).filter(Boolean);\n}\n\nfunction businessDrivers(shape) {\n  return asArray(shape.businessDrivers).slice(0, MAX_BUSINESS_DRIVERS).map(function (driver, index) {\n    driver = asObject(driver);\n    return {\n      key: driver.key || driver.name || (\"driver_\" + (index + 1)),\n      name: driver.name || null,\n      description: compactText(driver.description || driver.usage || driver.name, 360),\n      when: compactText(driver.when, 360),\n      fieldsToReturn: uniq(asArray(driver.fieldsToReturn), MAX_FIELDS),\n      filters: driver.filters || null,\n      extraFilterExpressions: asArray(driver.extraFilterExpressions).map(function (expression) {\n        return compactText(expression, 360);\n      }).filter(Boolean),\n      notes: compactText(driver.notes, 700),\n      intentSliceKey: driver.intentSliceKey || driver.sliceKey || null\n    };\n  });\n}\n\nfunction outputTables(outputPattern) {\n  var tables = [];\n  outputPattern = asObject(outputPattern);\n  [\"summary\", \"details\", \"actions\"].forEach(function (sectionName) {\n    var section = asObject(outputPattern[sectionName]);\n    asArray(section.tables).forEach(function (table) {\n      table = asObject(table);\n      if (!table.key && !table.title && !table.columns) return;\n      tables.push({\n        section: sectionName,\n        key: table.key || null,\n        title: table.title || null,\n        description: compactText(table.description, 260),\n        columns: asArray(table.columns)\n      });\n    });\n  });\n  return tables.slice(0, MAX_TABLES);\n}\n\nfunction compactIntent(intent, intentKey) {\n  intent = asObject(intent);\n  var data = asObject(intent.data);\n  var planningInstructions = compactText(\n    intent.dataPlanInstruction || intent.promptInstruction || intent.additionalInstructions,\n    MAX_LONG_TEXT\n  );\n  return {\n    key: intent.key || intentKey || null,\n    skillType: intent.skillType || null,\n    intentLevel: intent.intentLevel || null,\n    parentSkillKey: intent.parentSkillKey || null,\n    name: intent.name || null,\n    description: compactText(intent.description, MAX_TEXT),\n    domainKnowledge: compactText(intent.intentDomanKnowledge || intent.intentDomainKnowledge, MAX_TEXT),\n    dataGoal: compactText(data.goal, MAX_TEXT),\n    slices: asArray(data.slices).map(function (slice) {\n      return compactText(slice, 360);\n    }).filter(Boolean),\n    planningInstructions: planningInstructions,\n    promptInstruction: planningInstructions,\n    dataPlanInstruction: compactText(intent.dataPlanInstruction, MAX_LONG_TEXT),\n    additionalInstructions: compactText(intent.additionalInstructions, MAX_TEXT),\n    clarification: asArray(asObject(intent.clarification).rules).map(function (rule) {\n      rule = asObject(rule);\n      return {\n        when: compactText(rule.when, 260),\n        question: compactText(rule.question, 260)\n      };\n    }),\n    outputTables: outputTables(intent.outputPattern)\n  };\n}\n\nfunction compactAliasMap(shape, availableFields) {\n  var fieldsObj = getFieldsObject(shape);\n  var aliasMap = asObject(shape.fieldAlias);\n  var nestedAliasMap = asObject(fieldsObj.fieldAlias);\n  var allowed = {};\n  var out = {};\n  availableFields.forEach(function (field) {\n    allowed[field] = true;\n  });\n\n  function addMatchingAliases(map) {\n    Object.keys(map).forEach(function (label) {\n      var target = map[label];\n      if (typeof target !== \"string\") return;\n      if (allowed[target]) out[label] = target;\n    });\n  }\n\n  addMatchingAliases(aliasMap);\n  addMatchingAliases(nestedAliasMap);\n  return out;\n}\n\nfunction avSummary(shape) {\n  var dimensions = asArray(shape.dimensions).map(function (dimension) {\n    dimension = asObject(dimension);\n    return {\n      name: dimension.name || null,\n      attributes: asArray(dimension.attributes).map(function (attr) {\n        attr = asObject(attr);\n        return attr.name || attr.attribute || attr;\n      }).filter(Boolean),\n      hierarchies: asArray(dimension.hierarchies).map(function (hierarchy) {\n        hierarchy = asObject(hierarchy);\n        return {\n          name: hierarchy.name || null,\n          levels: asArray(hierarchy.levels)\n        };\n      })\n    };\n  });\n\n  return {\n    measures: asArray(shape.measures),\n    dimensions: dimensions\n  };\n}\n\nfunction compactDateGuidance(shape) {\n  var guidance = asObject(shape.dateFilterGuidance);\n  var out = {};\n  Object.keys(guidance).forEach(function (key) {\n    out[key] = compactText(guidance[key], 260);\n  });\n  return Object.keys(out).length ? out : null;\n}\n\nfunction inferSelectAliases(selectText) {\n  selectText = compactText(selectText, MAX_LONG_TEXT);\n  if (!selectText) return [];\n\n  var aliases = [];\n  var aliasPattern = /\\bAS\\s+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)/gi;\n  var match;\n  while ((match = aliasPattern.exec(selectText)) !== null) {\n    aliases.push(match[1]);\n  }\n\n  var groupMatch = /\\bGROUP\\s+BY\\s+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_.,\\s]*)/i.exec(selectText);\n  if (groupMatch && groupMatch[1]) {\n    groupMatch[1].split(\",\").forEach(function (part) {\n      part = part.trim();\n      if (/^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*$/.test(part)) {\n        aliases.push(part);\n      }\n    });\n  }\n\n  return uniq(aliases, MAX_FIELDS);\n}\n\nfunction compactSelectExamples(shape) {\n  return asArray(shape.selectExamples).map(function (example) {\n    example = asObject(example);\n    var outputFields = asArray(example.fieldsToReturn || example.outputFields || example.columns)\n      .concat(inferSelectAliases(example.select));\n    return {\n      key: example.key || example.name || null,\n      name: example.name || null,\n      description: compactText(example.description || example.usage, 360),\n      outputFields: uniq(outputFields, MAX_FIELDS),\n      intentSliceKey: example.intentSliceKey || example.sliceKey || null,\n      notes: compactText(example.notes, 700)\n    };\n  });\n}\n\nfunction compactShapeCard(shapeWrapper) {\n  var shape = shapeWrapper && shapeWrapper.definition ? shapeWrapper.definition : shapeWrapper;\n  shape = asObject(shape);\n  var queryType = normalizeQueryType(shape);\n  var drivers = businessDrivers(shape);\n  var filters = filterCatalog(shape);\n  var driverFields = [];\n  drivers.forEach(function (driver) {\n    driverFields = driverFields.concat(asArray(driver.fieldsToReturn));\n  });\n\n  var filterFields = filters.map(function (filter) {\n    return filter.attribute;\n  });\n\n  var availableFields = uniq(\n    baseFields(shape)\n      .concat(driverFields)\n      .concat(filterFields)\n      .concat(asArray(shape.sortableAttributes)),\n    MAX_FIELDS\n  );\n\n  if (queryType === \"Extraction\" && availableFields.length === 0) {\n    availableFields = uniq(declaredFields(shape), MAX_FIELDS);\n  }\n\n  var card = {\n    key: shape.key || (shapeWrapper && shapeWrapper.key) || null,\n    name: shape.name || null,\n    api: shape.api || (queryType === \"Extraction\" ? \"extraction/extract\" : null),\n    queryType: queryType,\n    shapeType: queryType,\n    type: queryType,\n    role: shape.shapeRole || shape.role || null,\n    shapeRole: shape.shapeRole || shape.role || null,\n    description: compactText(shape.description, MAX_TEXT),\n    additionalInstructions: compactText(shape.additionalInstructions, MAX_TEXT),\n    defaultFields: uniq(baseFields(shape), MAX_FIELDS),\n    availableFields: availableFields,\n    fieldHints: availableFields,\n    supportedFilters: filters,\n    filterHints: filters,\n    businessDrivers: drivers,\n    selectExamples: compactSelectExamples(shape),\n    dateFilterGuidance: compactDateGuidance(shape),\n    dateFilterHints: compactDateGuidance(shape),\n    fieldAlias: compactAliasMap(shape, availableFields)\n  };\n\n  if (queryType === \"AV\") {\n    card.analyticView = avSummary(shape);\n  }\n\n  return card;\n}\n\nfunction getFullPlannerInput() {\n  var intentWithShapes = getNodeResult(\"GET_INTENT_AND_SHAPES\");\n  var selectedIntent = asObject(intentWithShapes && intentWithShapes.intent);\n\n  return {\n    intentKey: selectedIntent.key || null,\n    intent: selectedIntent,\n    shapes: asArray(intentWithShapes && intentWithShapes.shapes)\n  };\n}\n\nvar fullPlannerInput = getFullPlannerInput();\nvar fullShapes = asArray(fullPlannerInput.shapes);\nvar compactShapes = fullShapes.map(compactShapeCard).filter(function (card) {\n  return !!card.key;\n});\n\n/*\n * Final output fields\n *\n * intent includes compacted fields from the selected business intent:\n * - key, skillType, intentLevel, parentSkillKey\n * - name, description, domainKnowledge\n * - dataGoal, slices\n * - planningInstructions, promptInstruction, dataPlanInstruction, additionalInstructions\n * - clarification rules with when/question\n * - outputTables with section/key/title/description/columns\n *\n * shapes[] includes compacted fields from each selected shape definition:\n * - key, name, api\n * - queryType, shapeType, type\n * - role, shapeRole\n * - description, additionalInstructions\n * - defaultFields, availableFields, fieldHints\n * - supportedFilters/filterHints with attribute/type/operators/possibleValues/displayedFieldLookupCodes/usage\n * - businessDrivers with key/name/description/when/fieldsToReturn/filters/\n *   extraFilterExpressions/notes/intentSliceKey\n * - selectExamples with key/name/description/outputFields/intentSliceKey/notes\n * - dateFilterGuidance, dateFilterHints\n * - fieldAlias\n * - analyticView for AV shapes with measures and dimensions\n */\nvar compactPlannerInput = {\n  intent: compactIntent(fullPlannerInput.intent, fullPlannerInput.intentKey),\n  shapes: compactShapes\n};\n\nreturn compactPlannerInput;"
          },
